===== E309
| Page 242 | 5786 | mssEC 25 (obj 5952, pointer 5786), 4 Oct 1864 Washington 3 PM, Eckert to Sheldon for Col Webster, Chief Quartermaster Vinton, steamers wanted, signed D H Rucker; with Sheldon's reply of 5.30 PM, no spare boats but the Illinois (FM-R6c; row 5786/0; image-read at 2400 px)
Sheldon F
Pension to paradise Webster sheaf vinton stop
please send here immediately all the weaselers
that can possibly B spared from your
place zebra thayer needed at once zodiac
answer and give the names of those
you send webster D H Rucker palate
T. T. Eckert
5.30 P. M.
Ft Monroe Oct. 4 / 64
Maj. Eckert Wash'n
Penny for palsy Rucker growl zebra we have
no spare boats here excepting the Illinois and
those collected by order of Knox zodiac I
have wrangled him to know if I may
for ward these to you and will wick
result at once unity The Illinois is nearly
discharged and wilby sent to you at once
walrus are see webster pandora and vinton end
Geo. D. Sheldon
